Managed in-memory caching service (Redis or Memcached).

```javascript
const redis = require('redis');
const client = redis.createClient({
  host: 'my-cluster.abc123.cache.amazonaws.com',
  port: 6379
});

// Cache data
client.setex('user:123', 3600, JSON.stringify(userData));

// Retrieve cached data
client.get('user:123', (err, data) => {
  console.log(JSON.parse(data));
});
```

Store and rotate database credentials, API keys, and secrets.

```javascript
const secretsManager = new AWS.SecretsManager();

const secret = await secretsManager.getSecretValue({
  SecretId: 'prod/database/credentials'
}).promise();

const credentials = JSON.parse(secret.SecretString);
```

Secure, hierarchical storage for configuration data and secrets.

```javascript
const ssm = new AWS.SSM();

// Store parameter
await ssm.putParameter({
  Name: '/myapp/database/url',
  Value: 'postgres://...',
  Type: 'SecureString'
}).promise();

// Retrieve parameter
const param = await ssm.getParameter({
  Name: '/myapp/database/url',
  WithDecryption: true
}).promise();
```

Key Management Service - create and control encryption keys.

```javascript
const kms = new AWS.KMS();

// Encrypt data
const encrypted = await kms.encrypt({
  KeyId: 'arn:aws:kms:region:account:key/12345',
  Plaintext: 'sensitive data'
}).promise();

// Decrypt data
const decrypted = await kms.decrypt({
  CiphertextBlob: encrypted.CiphertextBlob
}).promise();
```

